'' A FIELD INITIALISER STOPPED THE DECLARATOR LOOP, so every declarator after the first
'' was DROPPED. 'dim as short a = any, b = any' laid out as TWO BYTES with one field
'' where fbc gives four with two -- a wrong LAYOUT, so every field after it in the same
'' type sits at the wrong offset, and nothing said so.
''
'' '= any' is an ordinary expression here: it parses to an N_IDENT named 'any', exactly
'' as 'dim as integer i = any' does outside a type.
''
'' THE VALUE GOES IN 'c', NOT 'b'. On an N_FIELD 'b' is the BITFIELD WIDTH, so the first
'' attempt made 'dim as integer i = 5, j = 6' a FIVE-BIT field with j on top of it --
'' 8 bytes with both at offset 0, where fbc gives 16.
''
'' NOTHING READS THE DEFAULT YET: a field default is not modelled here or in the
'' name-first branch, so it is parsed and kept rather than applied. That gap is
'' unchanged; what changes is that the declarators after it are no longer lost.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-udt tests/mir/src/field-multi-declarator.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: s size 4 align 2
'' EXPECT-OUT: i size 16 align 8
'' GOLDEN: expected/field-multi-declarator.out
